Month = {JUN},
Abstract = {The World Health Organization (WHO) aims to ensure the highest level of
   health for all populations. Despite progress, increased life expectancy
   has not translated into a proportional rise in healthy life years, as
   chronic diseases are on the rise. In this context, health ecology
   emerges as a new scientific discipline focused on preserving health
   rather than curing diseases. It seeks to calculate healthy life
   expectancy by analyzing individual, social, and systemic choices,
   offering a proactive and rigorous approach to making informed decisions
   and improving long-term well-being.},
